  "executive_summary": "The National Cancer Institute's Clinical Proteomics Tumor Analysis Consortium (CPTAC) has generated comprehensive proteogenomic data for various cancer types, including clear cell renal cell carcinoma (ccRCC). While gene/protein regulatory networks derived from these profiles offer system-level insights, visualizing and navigating these complex, high-dimensional networks remains a significant challenge. Existing tools often provide static 2D visualizations that are ill-suited for interactive exploration or integrating clinical metadata. To address this gap, the authors introduce ProNetView-ccRCC, an open-access, web-based portal designed for the intuitive visual exploration of ccRCC phosphopeptide co-expression networks. The portal features a 3D network exploration interface built on the Three.js framework, allowing users to rotate and zoom through a network comprising 3,614 genes and 30 functional pathway-enriched modules. Users can interactively query specific genes, such as the oncogene ERG, to view their connections, associated phosphopeptides, and correlations with clinical variables like tumor grade. The tool integrates metadata from CPTAC studies, including pathway enrichment results and clinical outcomes, enabling researchers to link molecular network structures with phenotypic data. By utilizing standard client-side libraries like D3.js and Bootstrap, ProNetView-ccRCC runs on modern web browsers without requiring additional plugins. This resource aims to facilitate hypothesis generation and data interpretation for the cancer research community by providing a centralized, interactive environment for exploring the complex regulatory factories underlying ccRCC.",
